# Sensitive / personalized / time-valuable files — the Forge backs these up
# at least N generations deep (config/forge.config.json -> backup.levels, default 5).
#
# One glob per line, relative to the forge root (the dir containing this config/).
# Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored.
# Globs use shell globbing: '*' within a path segment, '**' for any depth.
#
# Rule of thumb: if losing it to an accidental overwrite would cost you real
# time, irreplaceable thought, or something personal — list it here.

# --- your own trained files & preferences (the heart of it) ---
profiles/**

# --- the knobs that define how the Forge behaves ---
config/**

# --- your reusable Claude Code / provider setups ---
presets/**

# --- the method & doctrine you refine over time ---
doctrine/**

# --- per-target intelligence you accumulate (recon, plans, evals, logs) ---
targets/**/RECON.md
targets/**/PLAN.md
targets/**/EVAL.md
targets/**/LOG.md
targets/**/target.yaml

# --- experiment records (hypotheses + results you don't want to lose) ---
experiments/**/HYPOTHESIS.md
experiments/**/RESULT.md
experiments/**/run.yaml

# Add your own below, e.g.:
# secrets/**
# notes/**
